{
  "name": "UberLLM: text to video with Veo 3.1 Fast",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Text to video with Veo 3.1 Fast (UberLLM)\nWrites a video from a prompt with Google's Veo 3.1 Fast, waits for it, and hands you the file.\n\n### Setup (2 minutes)\n1. Get a key at https://uberllm.dev (sign in with your email, add credit).\n2. Open any **UberLLM** HTTP node → Credential → **Create new** → *Header Auth*:\n   - Name: `Authorization`\n   - Value: `Bearer YOUR_UBERLLM_KEY`\n   Every UberLLM node in this workflow uses this one credential.\n3. Edit the **Settings** node, then click **Execute workflow**.\n\n### Price\n$0.1125 per second at 720p with sound → $0.9 for 8 s (price on 2026-10-30; live prices: https://uberllm.dev/fal-api-pricing)\nWithout sound: $0.075 per second at 720p without sound → $0.6 for 8 s (price on 2026-10-30; live prices: https://uberllm.dev/fal-api-pricing)\n\n### What you pay\n- The job's cost is shown before it starts (`max_cost_usd` on the reply) and held from your balance. It is never billed more than that.\n- A video that fails or runs out of time costs nothing: the whole hold comes back.\n- Credit you buy does not expire.\n- No UberLLM fee on requests. Adding credit by card costs 5.5% + $0.50.\n\n### The file\nThe last node has the video as binary `data` (send it to Drive, S3, YouTube…) and its link in `url`. The link needs your key and is kept about 3 hours. To have UberLLM put the file in your own bucket, add `output_upload_url` (a presigned PUT link) to the start request.\n",
        "height": 760,
        "width": 520
      },
      "id": "578dcc70-3053-5772-b359-88016d0dc47c",
      "name": "About",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -560,
        -260
      ]
    },
